  "verbalization": "Methylergometrine, a member of the ergoline class, is linked to Htr2c through its inclusion in ergolines, which are broadly associated with the nervous system. Both Bromocriptine and Cabergoline, which are also ergolines, bind to Htr2c, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the receptor. The lowest common ancestors of Methylergometrine and its downstream targets (Bromocriptine, Cabergoline) are categorized under \"Agent Affecting Nervous System\" and \"Nitrogen Molecular Entity,\" indicating a shared biological role. The evidence suggests that Methylergometrine may act through a pathway that involves binding to Htr2c, possibly through a common mechanism involving ergoline derivatives. The relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways converging on Htr2c, with the shared classification of these compounds under similar ontological categories.",
